{
	"id": "effect-is-a-description",
	"text": "An Effect is a blueprint, an inert description of a computation. To run an Effect, one must do so explicitly. If this sounds familiar, that's because this also describes a function. Functions are similarly dormant until they are called. This property, often referred to as laziness by programming language people, is deceptively powerful. In time, we will learn of its many fruits.",
